### API Gateway - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start order: Docker infrastructure -> eureka-server -> product-service -> api-gateway
### Every request goes to port 8080; the gateway forwards product calls to product-service.

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@api = {{gateway}}/api/v1/products

### ===================== GATEWAY =====================

### 1. Gateway health - expect "status":"UP"
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/health

### 2. Active routes - expect a route with "route_id": "product-service" and "uri": "lb://product-service"
GET {{gateway}}/actuator/gateway/routes

### 3. Path without a route - expect 404 ProblemDetail from the GATEWAY
#    (body contains "correlationId"; product-service never sees this request)
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/unknown

### 4. Correlation id is forwarded - expect response header X-Correlation-Id: demo-trace-12345
#    and the same id in the product-service log line.
GET {{api}}?size=1
X-Correlation-Id: demo-trace-12345

### 5. Invalid correlation id is replaced - expect a NEW UUID in the X-Correlation-Id response header
GET {{api}}?size=1
X-Correlation-Id: bad id with spaces

### ===================== PRODUCTS THROUGH THE GATEWAY =====================

### 6. Create - expect 201; Location header must start with http://localhost:8080 (the gateway!)
POST {{api}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "MON-BNQ-001",
  "name": "BenQ PD2706U 27 4K Designer Monitor",
  "description": "27-inch 4K monitor with accurate colours for designers and programmers.",
  "brand": "BenQ",
  "category": "monitor",
  "price": 549.00,
  "rating": 4.5,
  "tags": ["4k", "usb-c", "design"]
}

> {%
    client.global.set("gatewayProductId", response.body.id);
    client.test("Location points to gateway", () => {
        const location = response.headers.valueOf("Location");
        client.assert(location && location.startsWith("http://localhost:8080"), "Location: " + location);
    });
%}

### 7. Get by id
GET {{api}}/{{gatewayProductId}}

### 8. Update
PUT {{api}}/{{gatewayProductId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "MON-BNQ-001",
  "name": "BenQ PD2706U 27 4K Designer Monitor",
  "description": "27-inch 4K monitor with accurate colours for designers and programmers.",
  "brand": "BenQ",
  "category": "monitor",
  "price": 499.00,
  "rating": 4.6,
  "tags": ["4k", "usb-c", "design"]
}

### 9. Laptops under $1,000, cheapest first
GET {{api}}?category=laptop&maxPrice=1000&sortBy=price

### 10. Products from Apple
GET {{api}}?brand=apple

### 11. Products with 16 GB RAM
GET {{api}}?minRamGb=16&maxRamGb=16

### 12. Text search "gaming", 5 per page
GET {{api}}?q=gaming&size=5

### 13. Next page of the same search
GET {{api}}?q=gaming&size=5&page=1

### 14. Facets
GET {{api}}/facets

### 15. Backend error passes through unchanged - expect product-service's 404 ProblemDetail
GET {{api}}/does-not-exist

### 16. Backend validation error passes through - expect 400 with "errors"
GET {{api}}?minPrice=2000&maxPrice=500

### 17. Delete - expect 204
DELETE {{api}}/{{gatewayProductId}}

### ===================== FAILURE TEST (manual) =====================

### 18. Stop product-service, wait ~90 seconds, then run this.
#    Expect 503 ProblemDetail from the gateway:
#    "detail": "The requested service is temporarily unavailable. Please try again later."
#    Start product-service again and it works after ~30-60 seconds.
GET {{api}}?size=1
